          "created": 1794225804.2545831,
          "data": {
            "step": 4,
            "text": "The current implementation of `normalize_tags` only handles lowercase conversion and sorting, but it fails to address the full requirements: stripping surrounding whitespace, discarding empty tags, and removing duplicates.\n\nI'll fix the function to:\n1. Strip surrounding whitespace from each tag\n2. Filter out empty tags\n3. Convert to lowercase\n4. Remove duplicates by using a set\n5. Return sorted results\n\nHere's the corrected implementation:\n\n```python\ndef normalize_tags(tags):\n    # Strip whitespace, filter empty tags, convert to lowercase, remove duplicates, and sort\n    cleaned_tags = set()\n    for tag in tags:\n        stripped_tag = tag.strip() if tag else \"\"\n        if stripped_tag:\n            cleaned_tags.add(stripped_tag.lower())\n    \n    return sorted(cleaned_tags)\n```\n\nThis fix addresses all requirements while preserving the public function signature. The implementation now properly handles whitespace stripping, empty tag filtering, case normalization, duplicate removal, and sorted output.\n\nThe test case will pass as it verifies lowercase and sorting, which is now correctly implemented with the additional requirements.\n\nI'll verify this fix by running the tests.\n",
